---
/**
 * What "early access" means now that a test key no longer needs anybody.
 *
 * The page used to be a waiting list with a `mailto:` on it, because there was no sign up and
 * no dashboard. Half of that is fixed: `/signup` issues a test key by itself. The other half is
 * still true, and this page is where it is said plainly: there is no dashboard, no login, and a
 * live key still comes from a person.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, CONTACT_MAILTO } from '../data/site';
---

<Base
  title="Early access, Bookrail"
  description="A Bookrail test key is self service. A live key still comes from a person, and there is no dashboard yet. What exists today, and what does not."
>
  <div class="wrap prose">
    <h1>Early access</h1>
    <p>
      A <strong>test key is self service</strong>: <a href="/signup">/signup</a> sends a link to
      your address, and opening it creates the account, the project and the key. From a terminal,
      <code>npx bookrail signup</code> does the same and stores the key for you.
    </p>
    <p>What does not exist yet, said plainly:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>No dashboard and no login.</strong> The key is the account. There is no page that
        lists your projects, rotates a key or shows a bill.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>A live key comes from a person.</strong> There is no payment behind the plans
        yet, so live is issued by hand: write to <a href={CONTACT_MAILTO}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> and
        say what you are building and roughly how many bookings a month it makes.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>No payments.</strong> <code>payment.mode</code> other than <code>none</code> is
        a <code>400 not_yet_supported</code>.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What exists, and what you can read right now</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        The <a href="/docs/quickstart/">quickstart</a>: from a key to a confirmed booking, with
        the CLI, the SDK or plain HTTP.
      </li>
      <li>
        The <a href="/docs/api/reference/">API reference</a>, generated from
        <a href="/openapi.json">the OpenAPI document</a> the server itself serves.
      </li>
      <li>
        The <a href="/docs/cli-basics/">CLI</a> and the
        <a href="/docs/mcp/">MCP server</a>, both installable with <code>npx</code>.
      </li>
      <li>
        The <a href="/docs/concepts/">data model</a>, the
        <a href="/docs/guides/time-zones/">time zone rules</a> and the
        <a href="/docs/errors/">error catalogue</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      To delete an account, write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>:
      there is no command for it yet, and saying so is better than a page that pretends.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
